Read the portal color scheme before the first window opens

gpui starts every Linux client with a Light appearance and learns the
desktop's color scheme only once an asynchronous xdg-desktop-portal reply
reaches the event loop. The app's launch closure runs before that loop, so
on a dark desktop the first window is drawn light and then repainted dark: a
visible light flash at startup. Reading the setting once, synchronously and
bounded by a short timeout, seeds the appearance the first frame uses; an
absent or slow portal leaves the Light default, and the asynchronous
subscription still follows later changes.

